<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Magnus Erlingsson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1156–1184</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Magnus V of Norway</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Magnus Erlingsson (1156–1184) was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> from 1161, a son of the powerful nobleman Erling Skakke and a grandson of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigurd-the-crusader">Sigurd the Crusader</a> through his mother. With church support he was crowned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bergen">Bergen</a> in 1163 or 1164, the first coronation in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scandinavia">Scandinavia</a>. He was challenged by Sverre and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/birkebeiner">Birkebeiner</a> and was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-fimreite">Battle of Fimreite</a> in 1184.</p></div>
